WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.010
A grower tries a new treatment
on one row of plants,

2
00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.440
and leaves another row untreated.

3
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:09.060
Weeks later, the treated
row stands clearly taller.

4
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:10.560
The treatment works.

5
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.320
Or does it?

6
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:16.340
Then you notice where that row
sat: right next to the window.

7
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.760
So can you trust the result?

8
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.350
In this mission, you'll name
every variable in an experiment,

9
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.320
starting with a piece
of pondweed and a lamp.

10
00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.820
Then you'll time a paper disc
as it rises through a liquid,

11
00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.130
and turn that time into a rate.

12
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.800
A shorter time means a faster rate.

13
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.940
Your mission: decide whether
you can trust the result,

14
00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.690
and say exactly why.
